<title>ITALY: Italy's Perugia sees May CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Perugia sees May CPI at 0.3 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PERUGIA, Italy 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Perugia said its May consumer price index rose 0.3 percent month-on-month and 1.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In April, Perugia's inflation rate fell 0.3 and rose 1.2 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Perugia is one of 11 Italian cities to have published inflation data Tuesday and Wednesday. The city's CPI has a weighting of 1.26 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to April 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.3   (-0.3)    1.2  (1.2)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.1    (0.2)   -0.9 (-0.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.5    (0.1)    2.8  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0    (0.0)    2.4  (3.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0    (0.1)    0.1  (0.5)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0    (0.0)    2.7  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0    (0.0)    0.7  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.1   (-4.1)    2.5  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.0)    4.6  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  1.2    (0.1)    0.9 (-0.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 1.5    (0.3)    1.5  (0.3)</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
